# Generated cache of scraped pages (92 MB, rebuild with scrape_paleo.py)
cache/

# Creature photos: third-party assets, not distributed.
# Regenerate locally with descargar_imagenes.py
img/*.webp

# Private material: never committed, never deployed
.privado/

# The one-file demo, built by build_demo.py. It carries the creature photos
# inlined, so it inherits the rule above: the artwork is not distributed. The
# script that builds it IS published, and the demo needs .privado/ to exist.
amber-demo.html

__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/

# Superseded HTML artefacts of earlier game versions. They are kept on disk on
# purpose: the browser ties saved data to the file PATH, so each of these files
# is the origin its creatures were saved under, and deleting the file would
# strand them. Untracked so the repository carries only the current version;
# both are in the history, and nothing reads them any more.
#
# amber-jwa-3.23.html is in this list from 1-oct-2026: `build.py` stopped
# writing it and writes only index.html, because a versioned name creates a new
# empty store on every game update. The file stays here because n30's saved
# creatures still live under its path until he migrates them.
amber-jwa-3.22.html
amber-jwa-3.23.html

# A safety net, not a description. From 1-oct-2026 the dataset has a stable
# name, data/jwa.json, and the game version lives INSIDE it in
# `meta.version_juego`; nothing in the project reads or writes a versioned
# dataset any more, and one appearing again would mean the old scheme has crept
# back. The three that existed were moved to .privado/historico-datos/ and are
# also in the history (`git show v3.23:data/jwa-3.23.json`).
data/jwa-[0-9]*.json
/jwa-[0-9]*.json

# Personal working notes for this author; never published.
AGENTS.local.md

# Agent workspace: project memory and daily logs for this author; never published.
.workbuddy-ai/
